00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.000
We had made it to France. 

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
We knew the end of our journey was near, and our excitement grew each day. 

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:17.000
The last few weeks had changed us; we were now stronger, fitter, more adventurous in our flight. 

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:24.000
We particularly enjoyed following coastlines where we could catch the best winds to glide over the long beaches of Brittany. 

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.000
That’s why, at first, we didn’t worry when the wind started to rise that evening.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:38.000
We had been flying for about an hour. The moon was full and the waves were reflecting her light like a distorted mirror. 

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
The wind was getting stronger, but it was all a game to us. 

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.000
“You’re losing your balance, Bird!” Shouted Banjoko.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.000
“You wish”, I laughed, “I’ll race you to the end of that cape!” 

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:01.000
I spread my wings and accelerated. I could hear the wind whistling in my ears and my friend calling me, trying to catch up. I raced further.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Suddenly, a huge cloud covered the moon and darkness fell upon us. 

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.000
It started to rain heavily. Thunder was rumbling, and I couldn’t hear Banjoko anymore. 

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.000
I looked back, but he was nowhere to be seen. 

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Violent gusts of wind made it hard to keep my balance. It was so dark that I couldn’t see anything. 

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Then I heard my friend’s voice being carried by the storm. 

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:37.000
“Mawusi!” He never called me by my name. That’s how I knew how scared he was.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:44.000
Huge hailstones fell all around us, one hit my left wing, making me lose my balance. 

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:56.000
And then, I saw a light. A huge light, brighter than the sun, right in the middle of the night. 

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
“Am I dead?” I wondered. 

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000
As I flew towards it, Nunyati’s voice echoed in my head. 

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:20.000
“Follow the stars, Mawusi. They are the only lights you can trust. Fly away from all the others, as fast as you can.” 

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.000
I closed my eyes and called my friend. 

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.000
“Let’s land”, I screamed. I don’t think he heard me. 

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:35.000
I tried to make it to the ground, battling against the storm. I missed my landing and crashed on the beach. 

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.000
I dragged my battered body to a small cavity between rocks and decided to wait there.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:51.000
I waited all night, the wind howling around me. I was terrified. 

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:58.000
In the morning, the storm finally calmed down and I managed to go out. 

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:07.000
In front of me stood a huge concrete tower, a red and white striped giant reaching for the sky. 

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:16.000
I looked at it in awe, I had never seen anything like it before. 

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:24.000
And that’s when I noticed the tiny green shape curled up at the bottom, lifeless. 

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.000
My friend. 

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Banjoko.
